  "notes": "Fixes repair-action ownership in the fault curtain. A pending thermistor check cannot overlap another repair; dismissal invalidates its UI token and ignores its late completion while ordinary sensor sampling continues. Failed checks can be explicitly retried. Dismissal clears their presentation, and confirmed source resolution releases stale failure cards without clearing hardware latches cosmetically.\n\nSmoke-to-Cooling learning now keeps a valid start at uptime zero and measures durations across millis rollover. Invalid timing cannot become new short-puff feedback; existing learned penalty and flashlight records are preserved. The base model weights and safety thresholds are unchanged.\n\nIncludes a bounded passive-fault retry QA option that verifies source, focus, terminal failure and exactly one new action press. Build and host checks are recorded separately from live and physical acceptance. This release does not claim to resolve the previously observed intermittent BLE transport failure or complete every hardware QA path.\n",
